# Shadows of Thornwood

The road to Thornwood has been long and weary. As the sun dips below the treeline, you see the village ahead -- a cluster of modest buildings surrounded by a wooden palisade. Smoke rises from chimneys, and the warm glow of hearth-fires flickers through shuttered windows.

But something is wrong. The gates stand half-open. No guards patrol the walls. The evening air carries an uneasy silence.

You've come because Elder Mara sent word requesting aid. Strange things plague this village -- disappearing livestock, travelers vanishing on the forest road, eerie lights deep in the woods at night.

Before you enter, you should establish who you are.

